{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1548432-different-clans-different-breeds","id":1548432,"title":"Different clans, different breeds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-12T07:58:48-08:00","id":1548432,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Different clans, different breeds","content":"Hi! I'm looking for ideas and suggestions regarding the following: I'm trying to create a city were the vampire clans are weirder than usual, each clan is like a different species of blood-drinking predator that just happened to coexist in the All-Night Society. Folllowing the example of the proto-Mekhet and the posthumous Embrace, what sort of mechanical and flavor-wise ideas could I use to further differentiate each clan from each other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T08:41:25-08:00","id":1548435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1548432-different-clans-different-breeds#post1548432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi! I'm looking for ideas and suggestions regarding the following: I'm trying to create a city were the vampire clans are weirder than usual, each clan is like a different species of blood-drinking predator that just happened to coexist in the All-Night Society. Folllowing the example of the proto-Mekhet and the posthumous Embrace, what sort of mechanical and flavor-wise ideas could I use to further differentiate each clan from each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, maybe taking a look into <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Clan_(VTR)#Other_Clans\" target=\"_blank\">samples</a> from the multiples might be of help? Your comment on posthumous Embrace and i'm guessing Hollow Mekhet makes me think the Jiang Shi &amp; Grettir at least might fit on your interests.<br /> <br /> Aditionally, Mythologies, Danse Macabre and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Night_Horrors:_The_Wicked_Dead\" target=\"_blank\">Night Horrors: Wicked Dead</a> might also make for quite useful suplemental reads, the last one in particular having in its pages a number of peculiar beings that can blur the lines of what is or not a vampire.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Night_Horrors:_Spilled_Blood\" target=\"_blank\">Night Horrors: Spilled Blood</a>, how could i forget. It has some other obscure clans and an example of what might be another sort of proto-Mekhet. Really worth checking out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-19-2025, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T10:22:30-08:00","id":1548437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1548432-different-clans-different-breeds#post1548432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi! I'm looking for ideas and suggestions regarding the following: I'm trying to create a city were the vampire clans are weirder than usual, each clan is like a different species of blood-drinking predator that just happened to coexist in the All-Night Society. Folllowing the example of the proto-Mekhet and the posthumous Embrace, what sort of mechanical and flavor-wise ideas could I use to further differentiate each clan from each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>Going from the established material, vampires becoming Kindred is part of the larger phenomenon of the Blood tending to pool and run together from shared food and territory, so localized clans that are more differentiated from each other than Favored Attributes, Clan Banes, affinity Disciplines, and exclusive Merits are likely to have recent ancestry and/or activity further removed from interaction with Humanity.<br /> <br /> To this end, the city might have a relatively new or insular All Night Society whose clan representation comes from a small number of bloodline-bearing elders awakening from extended torpor (whose childer typically begin their Requiems already initiated into the bloodline), or there might be strict territorial enforcement and feeding restrictions between the clans such that even without the natural evolution of age and bloodlines some low-level speciation/specialization has occurred over the years. If none of the major covenants are present and Clan Status is more important to city politics this has more space to expand. Generally speaking, pulling further away from the base situation where fresh neonates are better off than revenants but not possessed of substantially more specialized powers means their sires are exerting a fairly high degree of control over their movements until they're more particularly developed.<br /> <br /> Alternately, you could lean into the game's natural mechanical space for unlimited granular development and have exclusive Merits and proprietary Devotions be more strongly represented among all the local clans; rather than an old and insular convention, this could be a fresher coup by a subset of the existing clans crowding out the less particular specimens in the area however many years ago as part of a specific agenda or suitability to some niche that is especially fruitful in this city, and this state of affairs hasn't existed long enough for time to start sanding off the hard edges of the clan's overall shape.<br /> <br /> Banes and ritualistic quirks below the level of a full Discipline are big ludonarrative arrows in your quiver for differentiation purposes, and if you want to tie them into the city specifically (in either causal direction) you might further link them with strange phenomena in the area. Maybe there's a gate to the Underworld that the local Haunts lair around that gives them all the ability to see and interact with ghosts, with their Clan Bane taking cues from Geist by gradually limiting their ability to communicate outside the context of fear with anybody but their Touchstones (or people who meet some other criterion). Maybe the local Serpents have adapted to literally feed on emotions and start to wither away if they don't have a Condition representing some strong sentiment. Maybe the local Savages begin their existence as a tiny animal that nests in their old body (like a rat or a large spider) and have to exert extra effort to control their human form before a certain point, but can extend that power to other human bodies. Maybe the local Lords are all geomancers that can use human sacrifice to exert gross control over their Havens and Feeding Grounds. Weird vampires can get real weird!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T10:49:26-08:00","id":1548440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1548432-different-clans-different-breeds?p=1548435#post1548435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, maybe taking a look into <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Clan_(VTR)#Other_Clans\" target=\"_blank\">samples</a> from the multiples might be of help? Your comment on posthumous Embrace and i'm guessing Hollow Mekhet makes me thing the Jiang Shi &amp; Grettir at least might fit on your interests.<br /> <br /> Aditionally, Mythologies, Danse Macabre and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Night_Horrors:_The_Wicked_Dead\" target=\"_blank\">Night Horrors: Wicked Dead</a> might also make for quite useful suplemental reads, the last one in particular having in its pages a number of peculiar beings that can blur the lines of what is or not a vampire.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Night_Horrors:_Spilled_Blood\" target=\"_blank\">Night Horrors: Spilled Blood</a>, how could i forget. It has some other obscure clans and an example of what might be another sort of proto-Mekhet. Really worth checking out.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an amazing help, thank you! I don't have the Clan books, but I do have the Night Horrors books, I'll check them out.<br /> <br /> I was thinking in perhaps replacing on the five clans with a single bloodline that has completely replaced said clan with their own numbers. The other four clans may have some bloodlines but not to the extent of completely erasing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T11:02:08-08:00","id":1548441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1548432-different-clans-different-breeds?p=1548437#post1548437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going from the established material, vampires becoming Kindred is part of the larger phenomenon of the Blood tending to pool and run together from shared food and territory, so localized clans that are more differentiated from each other than Favored Attributes, Clan Banes, affinity Disciplines, and exclusive Merits are likely to have recent ancestry and/or activity further removed from interaction with Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div> Exactly that, I'm trying something different with my next VtR one-shot and I'd like to present a somewhat insular kindred community where the clans have almost as much power as the covenants. Having some cosmetic and mechanical differences would help me to portray the idea that the vampire existence is a profoundly isolating and diverse experience, yet their commonality lies in their need for blood and who has access to the bes resources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1548432-different-clans-different-breeds?p=1548437#post1548437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To this end, the city might have a relatively new or insular All Night Society whose clan representation comes from a small number of bloodline-bearing elders awakening from extended torpor (whose childer typically begin their Requiems already initiated into the bloodline), or there might be strict territorial enforcement and feeding restrictions between the clans such that even without the natural evolution of age and bloodlines some low-level speciation/specialization has occurred over the years. If none of the major covenants are present and Clan Status is more important to city politics this has more space to expand. Generally speaking, pulling further away from the base situation where fresh neonates are better off than revenants but not possessed of substantially more specialized powers means their sires are exerting a fairly high degree of control over their movements until they're more particularly developed.</div> </div> </div> </div> Love all of the ideas so far! I'm thinking that the five main covenants have divided their territories between two neighboring cities separated by a river: the easternmost city has the Invictus and Lancea et Sanctum in power and the westernmost city has the Carthian Movement and the Circle of the Crone in power. And the Defiant don't give a fuck who's in charge as long as they are left alone with their research.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps I should team up the Invictus+Circle and the Carthians+Sanctified? Mmm, that would be a subversion of expectations...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1548432-different-clans-different-breeds?p=1548437#post1548437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternately, you could lean into the game's natural mechanical space for unlimited granular development and have exclusive Merits and proprietary Devotions be more strongly represented among all the local clans; rather than an old and insular convention, this could be a fresher coup by a subset of the existing clans crowding out the less particular specimens in the area however many years ago as part of a specific agenda or suitability to some niche that is especially fruitful in this city, and this state of affairs hasn't existed long enough for time to start sanding off the hard edges of the clan's overall shape.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1548432-different-clans-different-breeds?p=1548437#post1548437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Banes and ritualistic quirks below the level of a full Discipline are big ludonarrative arrows in your quiver for differentiation purposes, and if you want to tie them into the city specifically (in either causal direction) you might further link them with strange phenomena in the area. Maybe there's a gate to the Underworld that the local Haunts lair around that gives them all the ability to see and interact with ghosts, with their Clan Bane taking cues from Geist by gradually limiting their ability to communicate outside the context of fear with anybody but their Touchstones (or people who meet some other criterion). Maybe the local Serpents have adapted to literally feed on emotions and start to wither away if they don't have a Condition representing some strong sentiment. Maybe the local Savages begin their existence as a tiny animal that nests in their old body (like a rat or a large spider) and have to exert extra effort to control their human form before a certain point, but can extend that power to other human bodies. Maybe the local Lords are all geomancers that can use human sacrifice to exert gross control over their Havens and Feeding Grounds. Weird vampires can get real weird!</div> </div> </div> </div> Exclusive merits, devotions and banes, gotcha. That's the way to go! Thank you for all the great ideas!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T12:32:01-08:00","id":1548445,"title":"","content":"Supernatural merits can go a long way to give a sense of &quot;otherness&quot; to a character, even if most of them DO come from the clanbook.<br /> <br /> Of Rose &amp; Thorn is like unlocking a whole additional discipline out of Animalism, one that can go even crazier if one decides to mess with Mandragora &amp; Lacrima (ghoul pants and the vitae-like sap produced by those, both from the Ghouls book). Swarm Mind is freaky and can get even more so depending on what animals one can turn into. Those two plus Kindred Medium (from New Orleans: City of Damned) and Ghost-Eater (from Book of Dead) made my &quot;Gangrel&quot; (being someone risen from the dead through a pact with a strix-like black cat spirit made his identification as such...somewhat questionable) elder quite different from what many would expect one of the &quot;Savages&quot; to be like and something of a factor in his city's power dynamics and games.<br /> <br /> So much so he became a primogen much to the distaste of the recently enthroned prince - and his own, but that is another story. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That some of these same gifts would also be manifested by his childer only served to create more of a sense of a bloodline and entrenched heritage of strangeness among them.<br /> And the black cats - the dead and the damned cats (<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Skinchangers\" target=\"_blank\">kanaima</a>) could never leave them wholy alone. But that's what family is for, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-12-2025, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-14T18:13:55-08:00","id":1548507,"title":"","content":"That's hard with Predator's Taint; I have a theory that, there were five different instances of vampire-creation, and, over the millenniums, all vampire-blood commingled into one vampiric-blood, and that's why there's the 'Taint. <br /> <br /> And this would be a lot easier in the Masquerade, with Nos having an Appearance of Zero. Just enforce old V:tM clan-weaknesses. I.E.: Nos in the sewers, Ventrue in the manors, Gangrels on the outside etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}